@j4w8n - Renamed *safe* to just `getUser()` 😉

@ChrisChinchilla @mandarini  - I went down the rabbit hole. `getClaims()` doesn't actually solve anything, it creates more issues. Clearly, it still calls `getSession()`, which is an extraneous call, unless a `jwt` is passed.

https://github.com/supabase/supabase-js/blob/0afbf0037a135d5793e42b8b8eb5d06b16f2a845/packages/core/auth-js/src/GoTrueClient.ts#L3701

However, in our case, we need to get the JWT and parse it.  `supabase-ssr` should handle ALL OF THIS for us.

- Get `jwt` from token from cookie
- Pass `jwt` to `getClaims(jwt)` which should validate it, validate token, expiration, kid, etc
- Logout if something is wrong with token
- Call refresh token if it is expired to get new token (extraneous call)
- Save new access_token and refresh_token to cookies
- Logout if refresh token is expired


We should not have to think about any of this.  It should just be easy.  We call a function `getUser()` that does all of this. It DOES NOT call any extraneous call unless the access_token or refresh_token is expired.

It should, however, call the server for updating user info, password changes, etc (I think it does this now).

So, `supabase-ssr` needs its own `getUser()` function interally, something like:
```ts

export const getUser = () => {

    let { access_token: jwt, refresh_token, expires_at } = some_function_parse_cookies_internally();

    if (!jwt) {
        logout();
        return null;
    }

    if (expired < now) {
        const { data: refreshed, error: refreshError } = await supabase.auth.refreshSession({
          refresh_token: refreshToken
        });
        if (refreshError) {
          logout();
          return null;
        }
        jwt = refreshed;
    }

    // get claims checks expiration, kid, etc...
    const { data, error: claimsError } = await supabase.auth.getClaims(jwt);

    if (claimsError) {
        logout();
        return null;
    }

    return data;
}
```
Pseudocode obviously, but this should all be handled internally, and there should NOT be an extra request to the server unless necessary.

J

So I created a helper function for SvelteKit (this could be copied to other frameworks) that I think covers 99% of scenarios.
### app.d.ts
Add the `UserData` type for the reusable data. You could add custom claim information here as well.
```ts
import type { Database } from '$lib/database.types'
import {
	SupabaseClient,
	type UserAppMetadata,
	type UserMetadata
} from '@supabase/supabase-js'
// See https://kit.svelte.dev/docs/types#app
// for information about these interfaces
declare global {

	type UserData = {
		id: string;
		email: string | null;
		phone: string | null;
		user_metadata: UserMetadata | null;
		app_metadata: UserAppMetadata | null;
		role: string | null;
		expires_at: number;
	};

	namespace App {
		// interface Error {}

		interface Locals {
			supabase: SupabaseClient<Database>
			getUser(latestFromServer?: boolean): Promise<{
				user: UserData | null
				error: Error | null
			}>
		}
		interface PageData {
			user: UserData | null
		}
		// interface PageState {}
		// interface Platform {}
	}
}

export { };
```
### hooks.server.ts
We also need a common reusable `getUser()` function.
```ts
import {
  PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL,
  PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY
} from '$env/static/public'
import type { Database } from '$lib/database.types';
import { createServerClient } from '@supabase/ssr'
import type { Handle } from '@sveltejs/kit'

export const handle: Handle = async ({ event, resolve }) => {

  event.locals.supabase = createServerClient<Database>(
    PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL,
    PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY,
    {
      cookies: {
        getAll: () => event.cookies.getAll(),
        setAll: (cookiesToSet) => {
          cookiesToSet.forEach(({ name, value, options }) => {
            event.cookies.set(name, value, { ...options, path: '/' })
          })
        }
      }
    });

  event.locals.getUser = async (latestFromServer = false) => {

    const {
      data: claimsData,
      error: claimsError
    } = await event.locals.supabase.auth.getClaims();

    if (claimsError) {
      return {
        error: claimsError,
        user: null
      };
    }

    if (!claimsData) {
      return {
        error: null,
        user: null
      };
    }

    const { claims } = claimsData;

    if (latestFromServer) {
      const {
        data: userData,
        error: userError
      } = await event.locals.supabase.auth.getUser();

      if (userError) {
        return {
          error: userError,
          user: null
        };
      }

      if (!userData) {
        return {
          error: null,
          user: null
        };
      }

      const { user } = userData;

      return {
        error: null,
        user: {
          id: user.id,
          email: user.email || null,
          phone: user.phone || null,
          user_metadata: user.user_metadata || null,
          app_metadata: user.app_metadata || null,
          role: user.role || null,
          expires_at: claims.exp
        }
      };
    }

    return {
      error: null,
      user: {
        id: claims.sub,
        email: claims.email || null,
        phone: claims.phone || null,
        user_metadata: claims.user_metadata || null,
        app_metadata: claims.app_metadata || null,
        role: claims.role || null,
        expires_at: claims.exp
      }
    };
  }

  return resolve(event, {
    filterSerializedResponseHeaders(name: string) {
      return name === 'content-range' || name === 'x-supabase-api-version'
    }
  });
}
```
In the case we need to get the freshest `getUser` data from the database, which should mainly be cases when you need the latest row from the User table, you can call:
```ts
const { locals: { getUser } } = getRequestEvent();

// pass true for latest User

const { user } = await getUser(true);
```
You shouldn't need any of the other session information, as Supabase will handle this automatically. When the claim expires, `getClaims()` will automatically refresh the claim on the server under the hood. 

I've updated my [sveltekit-supabase-demo](https://github.com/jdgamble555/sveltekit-supabase-demo) repo for these changes.

This is how I believe the docs should use this for simplicity, with the exception of adding [Custom Claim](https://supabase.com/docs/guides/database/postgres/custom-claims-and-role-based-access-control-rbac) info to these types.

J

