Hey @mandarini,

Thanks for the quick reply!

I was referring to `getUser()` calling the server on every request, not `getClaims()`, but that was an old issue. I am also only referring to the documentation issue here, not my desire to have the internal code simplified. There have been several threads that have been already resolved.

Here are the current issues I believe need solved to close this:

1. [Flows - SvelteKit](https://supabase.com/docs/guides/auth/server-side/creating-a-client?queryGroups=framework&framework=sveltekit&queryGroups=environment&environment=remix-component) - `safeGetSession` still exists.
2. There are no Database Types in the SvelteKit example. You cannot correctly use Supabase JS without them. You need to create them and import them in `app.d.ts`:
```ts
import type { Database } from '$lib/database.types';
import { SupabaseClient } from '@supabase/supabase-js';

// See https://svelte.dev/docs/kit/types#app.d.ts
// for information about these interfaces
declare global {
	namespace App {
		interface Locals {
			supabase: SupabaseClient<Database>;
		}
```
with:
```bash
npx supabase gen types typescript --local > database.types.ts
```
3. And there should be an explanation on regenerating the JWT as it is NOT safe after certain changes:
```ts
await supabase.auth.refreshSession()
```

Yes, Nuxt and SolidStart examples need to be updated too, but that should be a separate issue IMO.

Thanks,

J
